<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The region under the curve <m>y = {3 x^2+3 x+2}</m> from <m>x = {1}</m> to <m>x = {5}</m> is divided into <m>4</m> strips of width <m>1</m>. Give exact values.</p><p>(a) Use the trapezoidal rule to estimate the area.</p><div>Trapezoidal estimate <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Use the mid-ordinate rule to estimate the area.</p><div>Mid-ordinate estimate <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find the exact area by integration.</p><div>Exact area <m>=</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/> square units  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Both rules add up strips of width <m>h = 1</m>. The trapezoidal rule joins the tops of the ordinates with chords; the mid-ordinate rule uses rectangles whose heights are taken at the middle of each strip. Integration gives the exact area.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{38}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{62}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{92}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) <m>A \approx \tfrac{1}{2}h\left[y_0 + y_4 + 2(y_1 + y_2 + y_3)\right] = \tfrac{1}{2}\left[{8} + {92} + 2({20} + {38} + {62})\right] = {170}</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Middle of strip <m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4.5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>y</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{13.25}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{28.25}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{49.25}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{76.25}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(b) <m>A \approx h(m_1 + m_2 + m_3 + m_4) = {167}</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>\displaystyle \int_{ {1} }^{ {5} } \left({3 x^2+3 x+2}\right)dx = \left[{x^3+\frac{3 x^2}{2}+2 x}\right]_{ {1} }^{ {5} } = {172.5} - {4.5} = {168}</m>.</p><p>The curve bends upwards on this interval, so the chords lie above it: the trapezoidal rule overestimates and the mid-ordinate rule underestimates.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>170</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>167</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>168</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>